{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Famous Artists", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Superstar Effect", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Looking to the Stars > Charlie Chaplin", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le06ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect and Past Simple tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.</p>   You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience. When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now.</p>     Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I have gone to Japan.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"seen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She has seen a van Gogh painting.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"buy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He has bought a van Gogh painting.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They have never heard of van Gogh.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You can use the contracted form when speaking:</br> I have = I've</br> She has = She's</br> He has = He's</br> They have = They've</br> We have = We've</br> You have = You've</p>  Find a list of verbs and their past participle forms. Memorize as many as you can.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Manner and Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is done.</span></br><br/><span class=\"italic\"> Example: She walked slowly.                     \t</br>How did she walk? Slowly.</span></p>  Many adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ly</span> to an adjective: </br></span></span>Examples:    \tsad - sadly, curious - curiously</span> <br/>  Some adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ally</span>: </br></span>Example:      \tcomic - comically  </span><br>The adverbs <span class=\"strong\">fast, hard, well</span> and <span class=\"strong\">straight</span> are exceptions.</p>  <span class=\"strong\"> Superlatives </span> <br/><br/>You use a superlative adjective to express the highest degree of a quality.</p>  You use a superlative adjective to talk about one thing or person in a group of things. You always use  <span class=\"italic\">the</span> with the superlative.</br> Superlatives can be regular.</br>  <span class=\"italic\"> the + adjective-est</br>       the most adjective</span> </br>or irregular", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good</br> bad</br> fine</br> quiet</br> pretty</br> lovely</br> valuable</br> intelligent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best</br> the worst</br> the finest</br> the quietest</br> the prettiest</br> the loveliest</br> the most valuable</br> the most intelligent\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tricky", "type": "name"}, {"content": "difficult to do or deal with", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's tricky to get a job in the theatre industry!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le06ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in an article about acting.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to crack", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to start doing or to enter into", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The industry is difficult to crack.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le06ob08aud02", "typ